title: Remove try_state(false) escape hatch from pallet-staking-async tests

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Removes the `ExtBuilder::try_state(false)` builder method and the
      `SkipTryStateCheck` parameter from the `pallet-staking-async` mock runtime.
      `Staking::do_try_state` now runs unconditionally after every test in
      `build_and_execute`, so tests can no longer silently leave broken staking
      state behind.

      Tests that intentionally corrupt storage to assert `do_try_state` returns
      an error must now restore the state before the closure exits. A shared
      `cleanup_double_bonded_ledgers` helper handles teardown for tests that use
      the `setup_double_bonded_ledgers` fixture. This is a test-only change with
      no runtime impact.

crates:
  - name: pallet-staking-async
    bump: patch
